<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mykhailo Hrushevsky</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1866">1866</a>–<a href="/years/1934">1934</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mykhailo Hrushevsky was a Ukrainian historian, author of a multi-volume History of Ukraine-Rus', and a leader of the national movement. In 1917 he chaired the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-rada">Central Rada</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyiv">Kyiv</a>, which proclaimed the Ukrainian People's Republic and in January 1918 its independence. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/radaa">Rada</a> fell he went into exile, returned to Soviet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a> in 1924 and died under surveillance.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mykhailo-hrushevsky.jpg" alt="Mykhailo Hrushevsky" width="320" height="501" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hrushevskyi_Mykhailo_XX.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
